 "drivingQuestion": "What does the inclusive language of the mishna cover for eating and drinking on Shabbat?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Both inclusions answered; Rava settles Ravina's question from the mishna",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.110a.5",
   "daf": "110a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "כׇּל הָאוֹכָלִין כּוּ׳. כׇּל הָאוֹכָלִין לְאֵיתוֹיֵי מַאי? לְאֵיתוֹיֵי טְחוֹל לַשִּׁינַּיִם וְכַרְשִׁינִין לִבְנֵי מֵעַיִים. כׇּל הַמַּשְׁקִין לְאֵיתוֹיֵי מַאי? לְאֵיתוֹיֵי מֵי צְלָפִין בְּחוֹמֶץ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ רָבִינָא לְרָבָא: מַהוּ לִשְׁתּוֹת מֵי רַגְלַיִם בְּשַׁבָּת? אֲמַר לֵיהּ, תְּנֵינָא: ״כׇּל הַמַּשְׁקִין שׁוֹתֶה״, וּמֵי רַגְלַיִם לָא שָׁתוּ אִינָשֵׁי.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «All» types of «food» that healthy people eat may be eaten by one eating them for medicinal purposes on Shabbat. The Gemara asks: The phrase: «All foods, what» does it come «to include?» The Gemara answers: It comes «to include spleen for» healing «teeth» and «vetch for» healing «intestines,» although they are not common foods. We also learned in the mishna: And one may drink all «drinks» on Shabbat. The Gemara asks: The phrase: «All drinks, what» does it come «to include?» The Gemara answers: It comes «to include» mixing «water in which capers have soaked, with vinegar. Ravina said to Rava: What» is the ruling with regard to «drinking urine on Shabbat?» Rava «said to him: We» already «learned» in the mishna: «One may drink all drinks, and people do not drink urine» and is not considered a drink. It is only consumed for medical purposes and is therefore prohibited."
  }
 ],
